uid "01e9553e-a36d-5ce4-9531-7c5e67d94d60" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494973 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186494406 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494973 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186494468 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494973 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186494702 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494973 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186494734 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494973 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186494790 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494973 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494973 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494973 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186494734 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494973 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "7b5c8af9-d959-569a-8058-100af23b2c12" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494998 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186494418 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494998 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186494479 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494998 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186494653 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494998 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186494797 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494998 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186494808 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494998 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494998 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494998 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186494418 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494998 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ae053587-50f1-5f8c-b674-29dc44c5f648" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495005 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186494404 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495005 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186494583 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495005 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186494665 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495005 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186494784 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495005 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186494796 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495005 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495005 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495005 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186494665 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495005 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "b725a1ed-492c-532e-82ae-acdc74378877" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495073 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186494998 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495073 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95228" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495073 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495073 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following vector spaces has a dimension of $18?$\n\nI. ${R}_{17}[t]$, the vector space of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $17$\n\nII. ${\\text{M}}_{6\\times 3}(R),$ the vector space of all $6\\times 3$ matrices over $R$\n\nIII. ${R}^{17}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495073 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "300def0f-69c7-5821-80a9-ead2c4071d95" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495073 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's examine each of the vector spaces in turn.\n\nI. Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}_{n}[t])=n+1.$ Therefore, \n\n  $$\n  \\text{dim}({R}_{17}[t])=17+1=18.\\,✓\n  $$\n\nII. Recall that $\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{n\\times m}(R))=n\\cdot m.$ Therefore, \n\n  $$\n  \\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{6\\times 3}(R))=6\\cdot 3=18.\\,✓\n  $$\n\nIII. Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}^{n})=n.$ Therefore, \n\n  $$\n  \\text{dim}({R}^{17})=17\\ne 18.\\,\\times \n  $$\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495081 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186495005 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495081 #edb/ref 1069 "q-106882" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495081 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495081 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the dimension of ${\\text{M}}_{6\\times 5}(R),$ the vector space of all $6\\times 5$ matrices over $R?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495081 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4868b354-15b9-5c4c-bfd0-122202f40c50" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495081 #edb/ref 1074 "The standard basis of ${\\text{M}}_{n\\times m}(R)$ contains a total of $n\\cdot m$ matrices, each with one nonzero entry that is equal to $1.$ \n\nFor example, the standard basis of ${\\text{M}}_{3\\times 2}(R)$ contains $3\\cdot 2=6$ elements, and is given by\n\n$$\n\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, for ${\\text{M}}_{6\\times 5}(R),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{6\\times 5}(R))=6\\cdot 5=30.\n$$\n\nIn general, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{n\\times m}(R))=n\\cdot m.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495107 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186494973 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495107 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95225" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495107 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495107 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following vector spaces has a dimension of $12?$\n\nI. ${R}^{12}$\n\nII. ${\\text{M}}_{3\\times 4}(R),$ the vector space of all $3\\times 4$ matrices over $R$\n\nIII. ${R}_{11}[t]$, the vector space of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $11$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495107 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "872bbc86-b2d9-5fc0-a340-666aa227cedf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495107 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's examine each of the vector spaces in turn.\n\nI. Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}^{n})=n.$ Therefore, \n\n  $$\n  \\text{dim}({R}^{12})=12.\\,✓\n  $$\n\nII. Recall that $\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{n\\times m}(R))=n\\cdot m.$ Therefore, \n\n  $$\n  \\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{3\\times 4}(R))=3\\cdot 4=12.\\,✓\n  $$\n\nIII. Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}_{n}[t])=n+1.$ Therefore, \n\n  $$\n  \\text{dim}({R}_{11}[t])=11+1=12.\\,✓\n  $$\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495165 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186494918 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495165 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95233" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495165 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495165 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following vector spaces are finite-dimensional?\n\nI. ${R}^{750}$\n\nII. ${R}^{\\infty },$ the vector space of infinite real sequences\n\nIII. ${\\text{M}}_{50}(R),$ the vector space of all $50\\times 50$ matrices over $R$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495165 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f0776bb6-a5c9-57f2-a5dc-9cd00549186b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495165 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's examine our vector spaces.\n\n- ${R}^{\\infty }$ is *not* finite-dimensional. To understand why, we first note that the following set of sequences is linearly independent:\n\n$$\n\\{{e}_{1},\\,{e}_{2},\\,…,{e}_{n}\\},\\,n\\in N\n$$\n\nwhere, for each $j\\in \\{1,2,…,n\\},$\n\n$$\n{e}_{j}=(0,…,0,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{1,}_{{↑}_{{j}^{\\text{th}}\\text{ position}}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,0,…).\n$$\n\nIndeed, we have that \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n}{x}_{i}{e}_{i}=0\n$$\n\nif and only if ${x}_{i}=0$ for all $i=0,1,2,…,n.$ Therefore,  for any  $n\\in N,$  there exists a linearly independent subset of ${R}^{\\infty }$ of size $n,$ which imples that  ${R}^{\\infty }$ cannot have finite dimension.\n\n- ${R}^{750}$ and ${\\text{M}}_{50}(R)$ are finite-dimensional. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}^{750})=750,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{50}(R))={50}^{2}=2\\,500\n$$\n\n \nare both finite numbers.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495209 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186495231 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495209 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6ac3edfc-26f8-589b-8f2c-b805c5ecd692" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495209 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186495107 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495217 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186495223 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495217 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7b787e2b-3bc8-5c8f-b9c3-b74f50bd3683" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495217 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186495165 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495223 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8c095d32-ef2b-570d-930d-b9c7020f763d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495223 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186495081 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495231 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186495217 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495231 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9ee124b4-4e89-5c70-ae8c-f8a1677ea468" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495231 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186495073 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495236 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186495209 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495236 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a70eb95a-1d4a-5112-b093-41836097c112" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495236 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186360586 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
